'<!-- Section properties of a solid ellipse: area, $I_x = \tfrac{\pi}{4} a b^3$, $I_y = \tfrac{\pi}{4} a^3 b$, section moduli and radii of gyration. -->
'<h1>Geometrical Properties of Ellipse</h1>
'<div style="max-width:120mm"><img style="height:112pt;" alt="ellipse.png" class="side" src="../../Images/mechanics/sections/ellipse.png"></div>
'Dimensions
#UI 'Semi-axis -'a = 2m', Semi-axis -'b = 1m
'Area
A = π*a*b
'Centroid
y_c = a'm,'z_c = b
'Perimeter (approx.)
P = π*(3*(a+b)-sqr((3*a+b)*(a+3*b)))
'Second moments of area
I_y = π*a*b^3/4
I_z = π*b*a^3/4
'Polar moment of area
I_x = I_y + I_z
'Torsional constant
I_t = π*a^3*b^3/(a^2 + b^2)
'Torsional section modulus
#if '<!--'b < a'-->
a'&gt;'b
W_t = π*a*b^2/2
#else
a'&lt;'b
W_t = π*b*a^2/2
#end if
'Radii of gyration
r_y = sqrt(I_y/A)
r_z = sqrt(I_z/A)
r_x = sqrt(I_x/A)
